  "_comment": [
    "The other half of the calibration: schedules that are merely late.",
    "The nightly's 09:23 slot was delivered 4h25m late — the worst delay this",
    "repo has actually measured — the market snapshot arrived 3 minutes after",
    "its slot, and Monday's weekly refit 2 minutes after its own. None of that",
    "is an outage: the data landed. A watchdog that pages on this is a watchdog",
    "that gets muted, so the assertion is LATE-or-OK and exit 0.",
    "",
    "Crons are the current, odd-minute ones. `now` is Friday 15:43Z, a watchdog",
    "slot; the 09:23 slot cleared its 6h grace at 15:23 and is the last due one.",
    "The two days before are clean — every slot delivered within minutes — so",
    "the same fixture replayed at 11:43Z, before the late run arrives, is the",
    "case a 2h grace would have paged on and a 6h grace correctly sits out.",
    "",
    "Runs are newest first, as the API returns them."
  ],
